    {
      "type": "barchart",
      "title": "Funnel \u00b7 device vs organic",
      "description": "Device = paired an Omi within 48 hours of first seen; other paired hardware counts as organic. It is a proxy: a buyer who never paired counts as organic, and pairing is itself an early success, so the gap between the two is overstated. Latest matured weekly new-user cohort, except Kept, which uses the newest cohort old enough to measure it. Onboarded counts only people who arrived on iOS, Android or Mac, the clients that report it. Install is not shown because PostHog sees nobody before sign-up; first summary is not shown because it has no event.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "yesoreyeram-infinity-datasource",
        "uid": "omi-admin-api"
      },
